  "_method": "Manual visual extraction by Claude reading captures/bts_typebar_resweep_cropped/<TT>_<NAME>_filled.png. Each entry pairs each FxItem-region address with the BTS label that displayed our distinctive write value. Sub-type byte (Param 1 at 0x10001103) was set to 0; values 1..12 written to consecutive Param 2..13 slots at offsets 0x07, 0x0B, 0x0F, 0x13, 0x17, 0x1B, 0x1F, 0x23, 0x27, 0x2B, 0x2F, 0x33.",
  "_blank_meaning": "Blank knob value: device clamped my distinctive value as out-of-range for that knob (e.g., enum knob with valid 0..3 received my 6 write → device shows blank).",
  "_screen_x_vs_address": "BTS often displays knobs in a screen-x order that differs from address order. typebar_full's earlier extractor read labels in screen-x and paired them with addresses in address order — that's the WAH/CHO/etc names-permuted bug pattern. The mappings below are address→label, so are valid regardless of screen order.",
