    "coverage": "100% — full row coverage including row-2 labels",
    "_resolution_note": "Initially 5 effects (0x02 AMP, 0x03 AMP_BASS, 0x1D DIV_MIX, 0x1E, 0x1F) were stuck because BTS UI didn't redraw on SysEx-only TYPE byte writes. Resolved via manual BTS drag (user dragged AMP, AMP_BASS, DIV_MIX into slot 0 sequentially), then probed the actual FxItem index BTS used. Discovery: dragging DIV_MIX creates a TRIO of FxItems — DIVIDER (0x1D) + SPLITTER (0x1E, internal/hidden in BTS) + MIXER (0x1F). That's why typebar_full had no 0x1E/0x1F entries: BTS doesn't expose those as draggable effects.",
    "_row2_resolution": "Re-ran tall resweep (320px crop) covering all multi-row effects. Got row-2 labels for all 10 previously-truncated effects: PEQ, SPACE_ECHO, DELAY_SHIMMER, FL_PRIME (+ BASS), REV_SHIMMER, SLICER, HMN, SITAR_SIM, A_WAH. REV_SHIMMER is the largest at 20 knobs (dual SHIMMER pitch shifters on top of standard reverb).",
    "_subtype_finding": "HARM sub-type cycle confirmed: addresses are STABLE across sub-types. BTS just hides/shows different subsets of the same address space when the sub-type byte changes. So the catalog labels are sub-type-independent — accurate for all sub-type configurations."
  }
